From: zhangjianguo <janegle@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: recover degraded capability read after hotplug

Unplugging the cable from an RTL8261BE can wedge the internal firmware:
the C45 PMA speed-ability registers then only report 100M. phylib runs
get_features() before config_init()'s vendor 0x145 reset, so the degraded
read permanently pins supported/advertising to 100M and auto-negotiation
can never reach 1G/10G again until a full reboot.

Detect the degraded read (no 1000baseT capability) in rtl826x_get_features()
and run the vendor reset in place before re-reading the abilities. This
recovers the XR1710G 10G LAN port after unplugging the peer device.

Signed-off-by: zhangjianguo <janegle@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -2539,6 +2539,47 @@
 	ret = genphy_c45_pma_read_abilities(phydev);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
+
+	/* A 10G PHY that reports no 1G capability has a wedged firmware:
+	 * unplugging the cable can leave the internal state machine degraded
+	 * so that the C45 PMA speed-ability registers only advertise 100M.
+	 * phylib calls get_features() before config_init()'s vendor 0x145
+	 * reset, so a degraded read would permanently pin supported and
+	 * advertising to 100M and auto-negotiation could never reach 1G/10G
+	 * again. Run the vendor reset here and re-read the abilities.
+	 */
+	if (!linkmode_test_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_1000baseT_Full_BIT,
+			       phydev->supported)) {
+		unsigned int tries;
+
+		phydev_info(phydev,
+			    "capability read degraded (no 1G+), resetting PHY\n");
+
+		for (tries = 0; tries < 5; tries++) {
+			ret = phy_set_bits_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND1, 0x145,
+					       BIT(0));
+			if (ret < 0)
+				return ret;
+			msleep(30);
+			ret = phy_clear_bits_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND1, 0x145,
+						 BIT(0));
+			if (ret < 0)
+				continue;
+			msleep(30);
+
+			ret = genphy_c45_pma_read_abilities(phydev);
+			if (ret)
+				return ret;
+			if (linkmode_test_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_1000baseT_Full_BIT,
+					      phydev->supported))
+				break;
+		}
+
+		if (!linkmode_test_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_1000baseT_Full_BIT,
+				       phydev->supported))
+			phydev_warn(phydev,
+				    "capability still degraded after reset\n");
+	}
 
 	/* not support 10M modes */
 	linkmode_clear_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_10baseT_Half_BIT,
